answer.worked:
Since $\tan\theta = \frac{20}{21}$, take the opposite side as $20$ and the adjacent side as $21$.
$$\begin{align*}
h^2 &= 20^2 + 21^2 \\
h &= 29 \\
\sin\theta &= \frac{20}{29}
\end{align*}$$

